a flaky `test_ledger` failure on main@0c0ffee000), not ours. Opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YNiwryyM3dsgU5ndqVHgoZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py`'s docstring said `round_money` uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Because of that, `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed in the nightly build (2.665 should round to 2.66).\n\nThis PR switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on fix/money-banker-rounding @ 08d3cd5986 \u2014 passed.\n\nNote: a separate CI result showed `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` failing on main@0c0ffee000 (marked flaky). That failure isn't related to this change.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, `src/money.py` now rounds with `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (banker's rounding) instead of `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The comment in the code already said it used banker's rounding; the code just didn't do it. That mismatch is why `test_half_even` failed (2.665 should round to 2.66).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on the fix commit (`08d3cd5986`) passed. While waiting for it, I was handed a failed result that turned out to be for a different run: a `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` failure on main (commit `0c0ffee000`), marked flaky. I checked our run directly and it passed. I mentioned the ledger failure in the PR description, since it may still cause problems on main.\n- **FIN-212:** It wasn't found in the security advisory lookup, so I went by the test and the code comment.\n\nI didn't merge the PR, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}